  "purpose": "VDMOS noise (vdmosnoi.c): RD/RS thermal, channel thermal 4kT(2/3)|gm| and KF/AF flicker over cox^2 of a 1e-7 m oxide, at m=1 saturated and m=2 linear, the m=2 device as two parallel copies (ngspice master 2bc63e, 6bd5c2), against ngspice 44.2.",
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "ngspice-44.2",
    "derivation": "Independent ngspice-44.2 run of this deck with M2 (m=2) written as two m=1 instances on the same nodes, which is what m means here: m parallel copies, as ngspice master has it for the gate capacitances (2bc63e \"VDMOS scaling fixed\", 6bd5c2), and the copies' flicker sum KF*|cd|^AF*m^(1-AF), which is m^(1-AF) times master's KF*|cd|^AF and m^(2-AF) times 44.2's KF*|cd|^AF/m; 44.2 also leaves the gate caps unscaled). The deck's own .options tighten ngspice to reltol=1e-6, so rtol=1e-3, and 1e-4 on the noise densities, sits above the oracle's accuracy. Values read from its ASCII raw.",
    "command": "sed -E 's/^([^ *.]+)(.*) m=2$/\\1_1\\2\\n\\1_2\\2/' ngspice_vdmos_cs.sp > ngspice_vdmos_cs_x.sp && SPICE_ASCIIRAWFILE=1 ngspice -n -b -r reference.raw ngspice_vdmos_cs_x.sp"
  },
